    "lore": [
      {
        "record": 999,
        "offset": 86664,
        "sha256": "edce6ba3f3778f69c52edbb8b3132719daba00c453efb2ea7b491a805fb741b4",
        "text": "The Launch Area is the Landing Pad."
      },
      {
        "record": 137,
        "offset": 31722,
        "sha256": "37fa6fa1961892bc27ced43ecfc388229bc20b544e3787c881791ff4ef25ec76",
        "text": "The Mauna build and design with no aesthetic qualities whatsoever. They have no interest in providing comfort either, at least for the plebs; although even the Elite class doesn't have much truck with the finer things of life.  Ugly concrete blocks with no curves or decoration, jarring to the spirit as well the eye, their buildings typify the Maunid Elite's approach to life; anything that has no immediate practical application is unnecessary and probably immoral.\n  The eagle-eyed observer might wonder why the Mauna, such a disciplinarian species, have no security facilities for wrong-doers. The answer is simple. It's because they shoot them out of hand."
      }
    ],
